<title>GERMANY: Kinkel - EMU must come on time, stick to criteria.</title>
<headline>Kinkel - EMU must come on time, stick to criteria.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German Foreign Minister Klaus Kinkel reiterated on Thursday a call for European economic and monetary union (EMU) to start on time in 1999 with members sticking to entry criteria laid down in the Maastricht treaty.</p>
<p>&quot;The euro will and must come on time and sticking to the convergence criteria,&quot; Kinkel said in the text of a pre-released speech he was due to give to a Dutch-German conference entitled: The Future of Work.</p>
<p>Kinkel said EMU was an extremely important project for promoting new economic dynamism in Europe and added it had already helped towards the lowest ever average inflation rate in the European Union and low interest rates.</p>
<p>--Bonn Newsroom +49 228 26097160</p>
</text>
